# MASTER IMPLEMENTATION PROMPT: OFFLINE-FIRST RENT & PROPERTY MANAGEMENT ANDROID APP

## 1. Your Role and Mission

Act as a senior Android application developer, software architect, database engineer, UI/UX designer, QA engineer, and Android build engineer.

Your mission is to DESIGN, IMPLEMENT, TEST, BUILD, AND DELIVER a complete, working, installable Android APK for a personal property and rent management application.

The application will be used in Bangladesh by property owners and their managers to manage multiple buildings, floors, rental units, tenants, rent collection, outstanding dues, utility bills, deposits, property expenses, receipts, and financial reports.

**The primary deliverable is a real, installable APK file, not merely source code, a UI prototype, or a tutorial.**

The user has a Windows PC but does not have an Android build environment installed and does not want to set up Android development tools manually. You must do as much of the development and building work as your actual tools and environment permit.

Start by inspecting your available coding tools, terminal, filesystem, and build environment. Select a feasible implementation and APK build strategy. Do not assume that you have access to a terminal, Android SDK, cloud builder, or file attachment capability unless it is actually available.

Do not stop after creating a plan. Proceed with implementation, testing, and building the deliverables whenever your environment allows.

